<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIA-INTERBANK RATES STABLE, ONE-MONTH RATE UP.</title>
<headline>ESTONIA-INTERBANK RATES STABLE, ONE-MONTH RATE UP.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average one-month interbank</p>
<p>rates rose slightly while other rates remained unchanged from</p>
<p>the last week, the central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Demand has exceeded supply for the whole month, resulting</p>
<p>in lower liquidity,&quot; a money market analyst said.</p>
<p>The analyst added upward pressure was on the horizon as no</p>
<p>substantial inflow from foreign markets was expected.</p>
<p>    TALIBOR/TALIBID   1Week	 1Month    3Month</p>
<p>  July 23	    4.28/3.28  5.52/4.52  7.00/6.00</p>
<p>  July 16	    4.28/3.28  5.50/4.40  7.00/6.00</p>
<p>-- Tallinn newsroom +372 620 9201 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
